{"nodes": [{"type": "group", "id": "111e53fc3a53492b", "x": -2646, "y": -1287, "width": 1255, "height": 1237, "color": "#89dceb", "label": "Comment \u00e7a marche", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "ad796e6d89974b24", "x": -830, "y": -2605, "width": 1660, "height": 1530, "color": "#cba6f7", "label": "Nutrition et chimie", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "9697780b671948b8", "x": 1053, "y": 379, "width": 1080, "height": 1080, "color": "#cba6f7", "label": "\u00c9volution", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "3320d78da29b458f", "x": -1878, "y": 1234, "width": 930, "height": 710, "color": "#cba6f7", "label": "G\u00e9ochimie et \u00e9cologie", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "bcabfc37647847e8", "x": 1840, "y": 1840, "width": 550, "height": 390, "color": "#f38ba8", "label": "\u00c0 ne pas confondre", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "group", "id": "f8894dbbb1964bc8", "x": -455, "y": 2670, "width": 910, "height": 510, "color": "#f5c2e7", "label": "Sources", "background": null, "backgroundStyle": null}, {"type": "text", "id": "eee217a1504044ee", "x": -2606, "y": -727, "width": 450, "height": 450, "color": "#a6e3a1", "text": "**Graphique**\n\n```tikz\n\n\\begin{tikzpicture}\n\\begin{axis}[\n    axis lines=middle,\n    grid=both,\n    domain=0:5,\n    samples=200,\n    xlabel={$x$},\n    ylabel={$f(x)$},\n    width=10cm,\n    height=8cm\n]\n\\addplot[blue, thick] {exp(-1*x^2)};\n\\end{axis}\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n\n```"}, {"type": "text", "id": "536fb33becc44ae8", "x": -2126, "y": -727, "width": 280, "height": 170, "color": null, "text": "### assimilats\n\nlumi\u00e8re, chlorophylle, H2O, CO2 \u2192 H+, e-, O2, assimilats (feuille)"}, {"type": "text", "id": "16e96893c76f4f23", "x": -2126, "y": -1207, "width": 280, "height": 170, "color": "#89dceb", "text": "### G3P\n\n\u00e9nergie emmagasin\u00e9e \u2192 G3P, ADP, Pi, NADP+"}, {"type": "text", "id": "d8b9d2a8c5014247", "x": -1711, "y": -967, "width": 280, "height": 170, "color": "#89dceb", "text": "### ADP\n\n\u00e9nergie emmagasin\u00e9e \u2192 G3P, ADP, Pi, NADP+"}, {"type": "text", "id": "f3dd3c374178422c", "x": -1711, "y": -488, "width": 280, "height": 170, "color": "#89dceb", "text": "### NADP+\n\n\u00e9nergie emmagasin\u00e9e \u2192 G3P, ADP, Pi, NADP+"}, {"type": "text", "id": "6c54d891f5624461", "x": -2126, "y": -235, "width": 280, "height": 145, "color": "#89dceb", "text": "### (CH2O)n\n\nCO2, AH2, photons \u2192 (CH2O)n, AO"}, {"type": "text", "id": "377481b1bba8474c", "x": -790, "y": -2205, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "### Organisme (physiologie)\n\nUn organisme (du grec organon, \u00ab instrument \u00bb), ou organisme vivant, est, en biologie et en \u00e9cologie, un syst\u00e8me vivant complexe, organis\u00e9 et est le produit de variations successives au cours de l'\u00e9volution. Il est constitu\u00e9 d'une ou plusieurs cellules vivantes (on parle alors, respectivement,..."}, {"type": "link", "id": "7956de5a47664e76", "x": -790, "y": -2525, "width": 400, "height": 300, "color": "#cba6f7", "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/E._coli_Bacteria_%287316101966%29.jpg/500px-E._coli_Bacteria_%287316101966%29.jpg"}, {"type": "text", "id": "2eb1b81b1308476e", "x": -340, "y": -2205, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "### Soufre\n\nLe soufre est l'\u00e9l\u00e9ment chimique de num\u00e9ro atomique 16, de symbole S. Membre du groupe des chalcog\u00e8nes, c'est un non-m\u00e9tal multivalent abondant.\nOn le trouve dans de nombreux min\u00e9raux (sulfures, sulfates et soufre natif), particuli\u00e8rement dans les r\u00e9gions volcaniques."}, {"type": "text", "id": "6e007d10a4f349fd", "x": 90, "y": -2205, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "### Plante\n\nPerturbation du processus de photosynth\u00e8se Le processus de production d'oxyg\u00e8ne peut \u00eatre inhib\u00e9 par des causes externes, avec par exemple une pollution particulaire importante ( a\u00e9rosols ou d\u00e9p\u00f4ts secs ou humides) qui peut interf\u00e9rer avec les rayons solaires (les bloquer \u00e9ventuellement) ou nuire..."}, {"type": "text", "id": "9f0b97294ed440cb", "x": -210, "y": -1785, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": "#cba6f7", "text": "#### M\u00e9sophylle\n\nLa fixation du CO 2 sur le phospho\u00e9nolpyruvate se d\u00e9roule au niveau des cellules du m\u00e9sophylle (partie sup\u00e9rieure du sch\u00e9ma ci-contre), tissu situ\u00e9 entre les nervures des feuilles , et l' oxaloac\u00e9tate form\u00e9 y est converti en malate par la malate-d\u00e9shydrog\u00e9nase \u00e0 NADP + ou en aspartate par l' aspa..."}, {"type": "text", "id": "d2d8aafd20884792", "x": 390, "y": -1785, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": "#cba6f7", "text": "#### Photoautotrophe\n\nPrincipe Les organismes photosynth\u00e9tiques sont photoautotrophes , ce qui signifie qu'ils sont capables de biosynth\u00e9tiser leurs biomol\u00e9cules directement \u00e0 partir de compos\u00e9s min\u00e9raux \u2014 le plus souvent le dioxyde de carbone CO 2 et l' eau H 2 O \u2014 \u00e0 l'aide de l' \u00e9nergie lumineuse re\u00e7ue du Soleil ."}, {"type": "text", "id": "8cbd57ab978344a3", "x": -790, "y": -1485, "width": 200, "height": 370, "color": null, "text": "#### Cas particuliers de photosynth\u00e8se\n\nCas particuliers de photosynth\u00e8se Plante au microscope \u00e9lectrique Animaux et photosynth\u00e8se La limace de mer , Elysia chlorotica , est le premier animal d\u00e9couvert capable d'utiliser la photosynth\u00e8se pour produire de l'\u00e9nergie."}, {"type": "text", "id": "69f78b9065bd44b9", "x": 1393, "y": 779, "width": 400, "height": 220, "color": null, "text": "### \u00c9nergie solaire\n\nEfficacit\u00e9 \u00e9nerg\u00e9tique de la photosynth\u00e8se L' efficacit\u00e9 photosynth\u00e9tique (en) d\u00e9signe l' efficacit\u00e9 \u00e9nerg\u00e9tique de la conversion de l' \u00e9nergie solaire en \u00e9nergie biochimique par la photosynth\u00e8se chez les plantes ."}, {"type": "link", "id": "746c319aaa5f4c2d", "x": 1393, "y": 459, "width": 400, "height": 300, "color": "#cba6f7", "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Two_black_light_lamps.jpg/500px-Two_black_light_lamps.jpg"}, {"type": "text", "id": "4252d87aaf2a4a73", "x": 1093, "y": 1149, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": "#cba6f7", "text": "#### Infrarouge\n\nLe rayonnement infrarouge (IR) est un rayonnement \u00e9lectromagn\u00e9tique de longueur d'onde sup\u00e9rieure \u00e0 celle du spectre visible mais plus courte que celle des micro-ondes ou du domaine t\u00e9rahertz.\nCette gamme de longueurs d'onde dans le vide de 700 nm \u00e0 0,1 ou 1 mm se divise en infrarouge proche, au..."}, {"type": "text", "id": "7a437507113d4acf", "x": 1693, "y": 1149, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": "#cba6f7", "text": "#### Ultraviolet\n\nLe rayonnement ultraviolet (UV), \u00e9galement appel\u00e9 \u00ab lumi\u00e8re noire \u00bb parce que g\u00e9n\u00e9ralement invisible \u00e0 l\u2019\u0153il nu, est un rayonnement \u00e9lectromagn\u00e9tique de longueur d'onde inf\u00e9rieure \u00e0 celle de la lumi\u00e8re visible, mais sup\u00e9rieure \u00e0 celle des rayons X. Les rayons UV ne peuvent \u00eatre observ\u00e9s..."}, {"type": "text", "id": "eb0b2fe684d5423a", "x": -1838, "y": 1634, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "### Membrane plasmique\n\nPyr\u00e9no\u00efdes Article d\u00e9taill\u00e9 : pyr\u00e9no\u00efde . (en) Repr\u00e9sentation de la structure entourant le pyr\u00e9no\u00efde de Chlamydomonas reinhardtii . [ 1 ] milieu extracellulaire ; [ 2 ] membrane plasmique ; [ 3 ] cytoplasme ; [ 4 ] chloroplaste ; [ 5 ] stroma ; [ 6 ] membrane du thylako\u00efde ; [ 7 ] lumen du thylak..."}, {"type": "link", "id": "aba2fc93106143ea", "x": -1838, "y": 1314, "width": 400, "height": 300, "color": "#cba6f7", "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Carbon_dioxide_3D_ball.png/500px-Carbon_dioxide_3D_ball.png"}, {"type": "text", "id": "4c34550c755943ed", "x": -1388, "y": 1634, "width": 400, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "### Ion\n\nLa photosynth\u00e8se s'accomplit en deux phases : une phase claire (dite aussi \u00ab lumineuse \u00bb) durant laquelle la feuille capte la lumi\u00e8re, qui associ\u00e9e \u00e0 la chlorophylle r\u00e9alise la photolyse de l'eau, c\u2019est-\u00e0-dire la s\u00e9paration des atomes d\u2019 hydrog\u00e8ne et d' oxyg\u00e8ne , et une phase sombre (dite aussi \u00ab..."}, {"type": "text", "id": "82fa75cf29824664", "x": 1880, "y": 1920, "width": 220, "height": 270, "color": null, "text": "#### \u2260 respiration cellulaire\n\nLa photosynth\u00e8se produit O\u2082 et glucose \u00e0 partir de CO\u2082 et lumi\u00e8re. La respiration cellulaire fait l'inverse : consomme O\u2082 et glucose pour produire de l'\u00e9nergie."}, {"type": "text", "id": "a0535e13723a45c5", "x": 2130, "y": 1920, "width": 220, "height": 220, "color": null, "text": "#### \u2260 chimiosynth\u00e8se\n\nLa chimiosynth\u00e8se utilise l'\u00e9nergie chimique au lieu de la lumi\u00e8re pour produire de la mati\u00e8re organique."}, {"type": "text", "id": "c2147342c0a74c7e", "x": -415, "y": 2750, "width": 400, "height": 180, "color": "#f5c2e7", "text": "Nature (revue)"}, {"type": "text", "id": "966b0cea3d5940f9", "x": 15, "y": 2750, "width": 400, "height": 180, "color": "#f5c2e7", "text": "Bibcode"}, {"type": "text", "id": "b2717c1161d7472b", "x": -415, "y": 2960, "width": 400, "height": 180, "color": "#f5c2e7", "text": "Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America"}], "edges": [{"id": "4c081336c94a4a07", "fromNode": "536fb33becc44ae8", "fromSide": "top", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "16e96893c76f4f23", "toSide": "bottom", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "cycle d'assimilation du carbone"}, {"id": "ee05d89033924698", "fromNode": "16e96893c76f4f23", "fromSide": "right", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "d8b9d2a8c5014247", "toSide": "left", "toEnd": null, "color": "#89dceb", "label": "cycle d'assimilation du carbone"}, {"id": "54a7db5a51c744d1", "fromNode": "d8b9d2a8c5014247", "fromSide": "bottom", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "f3dd3c374178422c", "toSide": "top", "toEnd": null, "color": "#89dceb", "label": "cycle d'assimilation du carbone"}, {"id": "e84a76b3e7a943d5", "fromNode": "f3dd3c374178422c", "fromSide": "left", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "6c54d891f5624461", "toSide": "right", "toEnd": null, "color": "#89dceb", "label": "produit"}, {"id": "a11a6d0774e044cb", "fromNode": "6e007d10a4f349fd", "fromSide": "bottom", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "9f0b97294ed440cb", "toSide": "top", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "composante de"}, {"id": "800470060fd2499f", "fromNode": "6e007d10a4f349fd", "fromSide": "bottom", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "d2d8aafd20884792", "toSide": "top", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "type de"}, {"id": "bd42f8a0ac944a1f", "fromNode": "69f78b9065bd44b9", "fromSide": "bottom", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "4252d87aaf2a4a73", "toSide": "top", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "se d\u00e9compose en"}, {"id": "e8e9cff4859e4f81", "fromNode": "69f78b9065bd44b9", "fromSide": "bottom", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "7a437507113d4acf", "toSide": "top", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "se d\u00e9compose en"}, {"id": "72956aee36234a60", "fromNode": "9697780b671948b8", "fromSide": "top", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "ad796e6d89974b24", "toSide": "bottom", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "\u00c9volution \u2192 Nutrition et chimie"}, {"id": "631dc9c2f4a5432c", "fromNode": "9697780b671948b8", "fromSide": "left", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "3320d78da29b458f", "toSide": "right", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "\u00c9volution \u2192 G\u00e9ochimie et \u00e9cologie"}, {"id": "f606dfd08fe74bd6", "fromNode": "ad796e6d89974b24", "fromSide": "bottom", "fromEnd": null, "toNode": "3320d78da29b458f", "toSide": "top", "toEnd": null, "color": null, "label": "Nutrition et chimie \u2192 G\u00e9ochimie et \u00e9cologie"}]}